<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Mallorca Guide: 16 places – coves without a road, mountain villages &amp; hidden gems – HiddenGem.Atlas</name><description>https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/</description><Style id="must"><IconStyle><color>ff4cd8ff</color><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="gem"><IconStyle><color>ffd0569b</color><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Placemark><name>1. Cala Màrmols</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · 🆓 Free to experience · Sturdy shoes instead of flip-flops, plenty of water, hat and sunscreen – there is hardly any shade. In summer start early. Stay on the official path: shortcuts across private land have caused trouble with owners before. And take a rucksack instead of a beach tote so you have your hands free on the steep descent. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o1</description><Point><coordinates>3.08981,39.28889,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Cala s'Almunia</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · 🆓 Free to experience · Bring water shoes, the rocks are sharp. In high summer the cove is no secret any more – early morning or spring/September gives you much more space. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o2</description><Point><coordinates>3.12642,39.32096,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Es Pontàs</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Enter “Mirador del Pontàs” in Google Maps – the entry “Es Pontàs” leads to a wrong spot or private land. Swim only in calm water and only if you are a strong swimmer. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o3</description><Point><coordinates>3.27777,39.46581,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Es Trenc – the long, wild beach</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Come in the morning or in spring/autumn; in high summer parking is the bottleneck. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o4</description><Point><coordinates>2.99511,39.34045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. La Seu – Palma Cathedral</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Take the photo from the Parc de la Mar in the late afternoon; inside the rose window is best in the morning. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o5</description><Point><coordinates>2.64817,39.56747,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7. Palma: Almudaina Palace, old-town lanes &amp; market halls</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Plan the old town for the morning and the markets as a lunch break – in summer the afternoon sun is fierce and many shops close for siesta. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o7</description><Point><coordinates>2.6476,39.5675,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>8. Bellver Castle</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Take a bus or taxi up and walk back through the forest – or the other way round if you want to be there early. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o8</description><Point><coordinates>2.61878,39.56386,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9. Valldemossa</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Come early or in the late afternoon and try a coca de patata at the baker. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o9</description><Point><coordinates>2.65503,39.64806,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>10. Sóller &amp; the historic train</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Set off in the morning; the last trains back do not run late, check the return times beforehand. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o10</description><Point><coordinates>2.69962,39.79948,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>11. Serra de Tramuntana &amp; GR 221</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · The roads are winding and narrow – drive early and allow more time than the satnav says. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o11</description><Point><coordinates>2.53427,39.51909,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>12. Sa Calobra &amp; Torrent de Pareis</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Go early or come by boat; after heavy rain the gorge is dangerous. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o12</description><Point><coordinates>2.80572,39.85226,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>13. Deià &amp; Cala Deià</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · 🆓 Free to experience · Go early or in spring/autumn, then you have the village almost to yourself. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o13</description><Point><coordinates>2.6489,39.7486,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>14. Cap de Formentor</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Go early in the morning or at sunset – by day in summer the cars queue. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o14</description><Point><coordinates>3.213,39.962,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>15. Qanat de Treurer</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Reserve, and arrive early enough to catch the terrace at golden hour. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o15</description><Point><coordinates>2.91124,39.53818,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>16. Wednesday market in Vilafranca de Bonany</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Markets are best early in the morning. Holy Week is fascinating but streets and parking can be closed or full then. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/mallorca/#o16</description><Point><coordinates>3.089,39.57031,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>
